index 00000000..4d994dd7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/DIVERGENCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,261 @@
+# Divergence from upstream (family-app fork)
+
+This checkout is the family-app fork of Vibe-Trading. It is kept as close to
+upstream as possible; every difference is listed here so a future upstream sync
+can reapply, adapt or drop it. The sync procedure is the repo skill
+`.opencode/skills/sync-vibe-trading/SKILL.md`; it reads this file.
+
+## Upstream
+
+- Original project: https://github.com/HKUDS/Vibe-Trading
+- Fork (this submodule's `origin`): https://github.com/thangtran3112/Vibe-Trading
+- Patched branch: `family-app`. The fork's `main` is a stale mirror (about 1,600
+  commits behind upstream) and must not be used as a sync target.
+- First fork base: `251b094320c1f97d1486626d3618113526914d4c` (upstream, 2026-10-04)
+
+The `upstream` remote is not part of a clone. Add it with exactly:
+
+```
+git remote add upstream https://github.com/HKUDS/Vibe-Trading.git
+```
+
+## Why
+
+Release 1 of the Trading Hub runs Vibe on direct OpenAI only. Upstream's Settings
+page offered a fixed list of reasoning efforts for every model, so it could save
+a value the model rejects, and the saved value then failed every run:
+
+    provider_stream_error provider=openai model=gpt-6.1-sol: ... 400 ...
+    'reasoning_effort' does not support 'max' with this model.
+    Supported values are: 'low', 'medium', 'high', and 'xhigh'.
+
+The owner also asked for the default OpenAI model to be Sol, and for temperature,
+QVeris and the China data-source credentials to be removed from Settings.
+
+Release 1 research quality (sub-projects 1 and 2 of
+`ai-trading/plans/subplans/01n-vibe-research-quality.md`): on real US-stock
+research runs the grounding gate cut figures, or replaced the whole answer,
+for numbers it could not verify. None of ten baseline runs finished clean.
+The gate now keeps and marks declared unverifiable figures `(unverified※)`,
+deterministic false rejections are repaired, and the profile tool exposes
+consensus fields it used to drop. The owner rejected Jina Reader entirely:
+`read_url` is absent from local/MCP catalogs, its bundled skill is gone,
+and the compatibility function makes no network request. A safe replacement
+reader requires a separate design. Per-message reasoning effort is the
+other change in this batch; each difference has a row below.
+
+## Changes
+
+`agent/backtest/` differs only in Yahoo's read-only split-event check (SP4).
+The research-quality changes below touch grounding, prompt, data tools and
+the published tool/skill catalogs.
+
+### Backend (`agent/`)
+
+| Path | Change | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| `src/api/settings_routes.py` | New `POST /settings/llm/reasoning-efforts` and `_discover_reasoning_efforts()`. It sends one chat-completions request with a deliberately invalid `reasoning_effort`; OpenAI rejects it before generating (no tokens) and the error names the values that model accepts. Direct OpenAI only (host must be `api.openai.com`); any other provider, a missing key, or an unparseable answer gives the fallback `low, medium, high` with `source: "default"`. A model that has no reasoning control gives `[]`. | The picker must follow the model. Never hardcode a per-model table: it goes stale with each OpenAI release. |
+| `src/api/settings_routes.py` | `_discover_reasoning_efforts` trusts only the model-specific error form (generic supported-value lists incorrectly offer `xhigh` for `o3`) and caches definite answers for ten minutes by provider/model/base URL. New `validate_reasoning_effort()` and `validate_message_reasoning_effort()` share the same refusal logic between Settings and per-message validation. Tests: `tests/test_settings_api.py` (cache-clearing fixture and ten new cases). | Opening a chat and sending a message need not probe twice; an inconclusive answer must never be cached or claim unsupported levels. |
+| `src/providers/llm.py`, `src/providers/chat.py` | `build_llm`/`ChatLLM` accept an optional per-call `reasoning_effort`, preferred over environment in openai-codex, anthropic and OpenAI-compatible branches; `_effective_effort()` normalizes it. `ChatLLM.runtime_snapshot.reasoning_effort` reports the effective value. Tests: `test_reasoning_effort_override.py`. | Every downstream reply and committee consumer reads the snapshot; concurrent chats never mutate shared config. |
+| `src/api/sessions_routes.py` | `SendMessageRequest.reasoning_effort` is normalized and validated by `validate_message_reasoning_effort` before the user message is stored or an attempt created. Omitted/empty means server default. | Owner request: effort set in the chat per message, without a failed run for rejected input. |
+| `src/api/sessions_routes.py`, `tests/test_goal_api.py` | `GET /sessions/{id}/goal` returns 200 JSON null for an existing chat without an active goal (including cancelled), while unknown sessions still return 404; active goals still return their snapshot. | Owner-approved browser-gate repair: the ordinary-chat 404 was expected by old API but appeared as a failed request and console error on every no-goal chat. |
+| `src/session/service.py`, `src/tools/__init__.py` | `send_message` → `_run_attempt` → `_run_with_agent` explicitly pass the override to `ChatLLM` and accept it at `build_registry` (Task 4 threads it onward to committee workers). Not stored on `Attempt`. | No process-wide config mutation; startup recovery does not rerun interrupted attempts. |
+| `tests/test_reasoning_effort_message_validation.py`, `tests/test_reasoning_effort_service_threading.py`, `tests/test_session_tool_trail.py`, `tests/test_session_service_mcp.py` | New route and service-threading tests; two pre-existing ChatLLM fakes accept keyword arguments. | Pin the before-storage and per-run threading contracts. |
+| `src/tools/__init__.py`, `src/tools/swarm_tool.py`, `src/swarm/runtime.py`, `src/swarm/worker.py` | Thread `reasoning_effort` from the chat registry through `SwarmTool`, `SwarmRuntime.start_run` / `_execute_run` / `_execute_layer` / `_run_worker_with_retries`, to each worker's `ChatLLM`. `run.reasoning_effort` records the override, or the environment default when omitted. | Committee review must use and record the chat's selected level on every agent, not just the parent chat. |
+| `src/swarm/runtime.py`, `src/swarm/presets/investment_committee.yaml`, `tests/test_swarm_run_metadata.py` | Generated committee run ID overrides any caller-supplied value before persistence; the US chair receives that ID and host-provided independent consensus context, and must end its report with one typed disposition. | A terminal-completed swarm or forged run ID cannot by itself authorize an own Buy/Sell/target. |
+| `src/agent/committee_gate.py`, `tests/test_committee_gate.py` | Validate run/ticker/parent-run association, four completed reviewers, typed chair rationale, independent source periods/counts and SEC/quote/split target math; require the chair's EPS to match the filed SEC fact and use Yahoo's actual source quote time, not fetch time. Give the chair checked EPS/quote inputs, then persist/render their dates, horizon, assumptions and confidence range (regression: source quote Friday, retrieved Monday). Use a fixed-host authenticated bridge client that rejects redirects and ignores host proxies, and render only checked typed fields. | Own US-stock recommendations need auditable, reproducible server-calculated targets; a stale quote refreshed today is still stale, and internal auth must never transit an inherited HTTP proxy. |
+| `src/tools/stock_profile_tool.py`, `tests/test_stock_profile_tool.py` | Preserve Yahoo `price.regularMarketTime` as the compact listing's `quote_timestamp`; leave its current price and analyst trend fields unchanged. | Retrieval time is not market quote time; only the provider's timestamp can date a share-price input to own valuation math. |
+| `src/agent/committee_gate.py`, `src/agent/loop.py`, `src/agent/grounding/ledger.py`, `src/session/service.py`, `tests/test_committee_gate_stream.py`, `tests/test_grounding_release.py`, `tests/test_session_tool_trail.py`, `tests/test_session_restart_recovery.py` | One per-turn policy buffers US-stock answer text and reasoning tails, including implicit analyst/earnings questions without a ticker, starts at most one host-controlled committee for own intent (distinct from attributed analyst queries in English/Chinese); “buy-and-hold” as a backtest benchmark does not request an own Buy/Hold verdict. It independently classifies free prose and accepts the exact SHA-256 of the already-grounded release. Both clean releases (including a removed figures declaration, recorded without a spurious revalidated flag) and deliberate `(unverified※)` flags now have a release hash; only changed text is revalidated before resorting to at most two rewrites. The independently checked typed approval is appended afterward. When an attempted automatic committee either lacked corroboration or approved a checked verdict, two observed false model claims that its runner was unavailable are replaced with the corresponding true host status without dropping the rest of the checked analysis. Model-supplied decision tags/JSON cannot masquerade as neutral prose. A metadata-only release-check verdict and bounded, literal check-stage codes are persisted in the trace; no hidden text is logged. First-person own advice is blocked even when the same sentence also mentions attributed analyst data. The same sanitizer runs before AgentLoop callbacks and direct SwarmTool callbacks in SessionService, before checkpoint/SSE/tool trail; late manual swarm events remain sanitized after parent release. Sanitized swarm stages map to existing `tool_progress` UI with a synthetic committee tool call, never an exposed raw run ID. The parent stall watchdog respects the finite SwarmTool wait budget, then resumes with fresh activity; heartbeats still do not mask other stalled tools. Stop returns promptly while a running committee worker may finish privately; SP5 owns durable recovery. Explicit non-US resolutions regain the prior stream behavior. | No unreviewed own verdict or target reaches a browser, CLI/MCP result, saved reply or reconnect checkpoint; safe, grounded analysis is not needlessly discarded by a generative rewrite. |
+| `src/tools/swarm_tool.py`, `src/agent/committee_gate.py`, `tests/test_swarm_route_contracts.py` | Server-owned automatic committees write beneath the separate `.committee` subtree using a per-execution context flag; concurrent manually launched swarms keep the ordinary public REST/MCP store. The gate verifies private run artifacts. | An authenticated `/swarm/runs/{id}` or `/swarm/runs/{id}/events` request must not bypass chat quarantine by returning an unreviewed chair report, even when both kinds of run overlap. |
+| `src/agent/committee_gate.py`, `tests/test_committee_gate_stream.py` | Final-answer scanner treats “buy-and-hold SPY benchmark” as a benchmark, not an own Hold instruction; standalone “Buy-and-hold SPY,” “Hold SPY now” and “Buy-and-hold SPY now” remain unsafe. | A backtest must not lose grounded results merely because its comparison benchmark sounds like a trading command, without permitting an imperative own recommendation. |
+| `src/agent/trace.py`, `src/agent/grounding/ledger.py` | Quarantined US-stock traces redact text before sidecar offload and persist only check hashes/codes; live in-memory evidence still backs the server's proof. | Hidden drafts must not survive in trace or grounding artifacts and become downloadable later. |
