+- **Browser:** isolated local browser showed “Default (Extra high)”, model-specific options, 44px keyboard-focusable select with “Applies from your next message” accessible description. Selecting Low sent `reasoning_effort=low`; while a subsequent High research run streamed the selector was disabled and displayed High, and its POST body and final metadata both reported `high`. Reload restored the prior Low choice from completed reply metadata. `zh-CN` showed `默认（极高）`; `ar` showed `الافتراضي (مرتفع جدًا)` in an RTL document. At 390px the control remained in viewport with no horizontal scroll. Initial browser pass exposed a pre-existing 404 for ordinary chats without a research goal. Owner approved the bounded API repair (`c9d2029`): fresh browser pass against the new server returned 200 JSON null for both existing no-goal and newly created chats; reload, Chinese/Arabic labels and RTL rechecked; **0 console errors, 0 unexpected 4xx/5xx**. Unknown-session 404 remains intentional and tested.
+- **Known picker limit:** with an inconclusive probe after a Settings model change, a previously chosen level that is absent from the fallback options stays pending per the approved policy. The native select can look unselected while the old level is still sent; a generic-list model may reject it at runtime. Do not claim the fallback verifies that level. Explicitly surfacing this state belongs with sub-project 2b's chat model picker; no unverified levels are added to the offered list here.
